WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.000
Organizations do not necessarily implement every control in the catalog.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.220
NIST supports a risk-based approach that allows organizations to select and tailor

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.620
controls based on mission needs,

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:13.045
regulatory requirements, system impact, and risk tolerance.

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:15.015
Control baselines provide starting points.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:18.415
A baseline can help teams avoid beginning with an empty page when deciding which

00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:20.000
safeguards may apply to a system.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.990
Tailoring adjusts the starting point to fit the actual environment.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.850
Organizations may add controls, refine parameters, document exceptions,

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:31.990
or apply overlays based on mission, threat, law, policy, and system characteristics.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:32.810
Good tailoring is accountable.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:35.110
Decisions should be documented, justified,

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.760
and connected to risk rather than treated as informal preference.
